    "body": "This reads as if you do not really want to allow a command to return 0. In that case, would it make sense to define 0 as \"No previous operation\" so it can _only_ be used as the reset default.\n\nAlso, is it safe for software to assume that all reserved/custom encodings correspond to failure cases? If not, should there be separate ranges for success/failure status codes?",
