      "type": "User",
      "user_view_type": "public",
      "site_admin": false
    },
    "body": "A status code of 0 can be returned. The recommendation is to use a defined code where possible and fall back to the unspecified code only if it cannot be mapped to a defined code.\r\n\r\nReserved encodings are reserved and must not be used. Any future use of reserved encodings would be with an opt-in so legacy software will not be surprised as they cannot be produced unless explicitly enabled. At the moment we would not want to designate all of those as failure codes to allow flexibility for future extensions.\r\n\r\nCustom encodings are implementation specific and the rules related to those are implementation defined.",
